 "section_summary": "This section comprises pages 16 through 85 of an official roster of Japanese educational institutions located in Osaka Prefecture, documenting prefectural and municipal schools as of 1946. It provides detailed tables listing school names, addresses, founding dates, male and female enrollment figures, and full-time and part-time teacher counts as of April 30, 1946, and November 30, 1946. The institutions covered include secondary vocational, agricultural, technical, middle, and girls' high schools; municipal colleges and youth schools; an extensive directory of municipal elementary schools; municipal kindergartens; and special schools for the blind and deaf-mute. Explanatory footnotes document fluctuations in enrollment and staffing resulting from wartime student evacuations and returns, post-demobilization teacher retirements, boundary reorganizations, and school consolidations.",
