   "summary": "This section contains pages 16 through 85 of a comprehensive roster detailing public educational institutions throughout Osaka Prefecture as of 1946. The tables record institution names, municipal and prefectural affiliations, locations, founding dates, student enrollment broken down by gender, and counts of full-time and part-time teachers as of April 30 and November 30, 1946. Covered facilities include secondary vocational, technical, agricultural, middle, and girls' high schools; municipal colleges and youth schools; an extensive directory of municipal elementary schools; municipal kindergartens; and prefectural and municipal special schools for the blind and deaf-mute. Accompanying annotations provide context on student enrollment changes, boundary shifts, school mergers, and post-repatriation teacher retirements.",
